Jeremy Conway &#x2014; an artiste&#x2019;s agent, and a titan of the industry with an unerring eye for the stars of the future &#x2014; died earlier this month aged 87. His client list was legendary, a rollcall that included Anthony Hopkins , Brian Cox, Helena Bonham Carter , Benedict Cumberbatch, Claire Bloom, Greta Scacchi, Noma Dumezweni, Joanne Froggatt, and David Harewood,.

Over 50 years ago, Conway founded his eponymous agency. In 1980, Nicki Van Gelder joined him, adding her name to the shingle. There were just three of them in the office then, and when John Grant joined in 1994 there were nine. &#x201C;We are now 32!&#x201D; Grant recently told Deadline of the company that&#x2019;s now a powerhouse called Conway Van Gelder Grant . Grant confirmed that Conway &#x2014; &#x201C;his friend and mentor&#x201D; &#x2014; had died on 1 November this year. Conway was CVGG&#x2019;s principal partner until he retired in 2015. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article1-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid","mid-articleX","mid-article","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[2,2],[300,250],[620,350],[300,251],[501,282],[3,3],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories News Breaking Baz: 'Bunker' Writer-Director Florian Zeller Takes Us Behind The Scenes With Penélope Cruz, Javier Bardem, Stephen Graham & Dame Eileen Atkins News Anthony Hopkins To Star In Post-Apocalyptic Sci-Fi '2048' -- TIFF Market

In a tribute penned for Deadline, Bonham Carter, who&#x2019;s still with the agency, recalled a note she had written for Conway&#x2019;s retirement party thanking him &#x201C;for my career.&#x201D; She meant it. She continued, &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t think any of it would have happened if it weren&#x2019;t for him. He started it all; 42 years ago, I was 17 and sitting in Jeremy&#x2019;s office on a rather low futon or sofa watching him pace up and down in front of me in mild frustration. He had seen me in a Channel 4 drama playing an Edwardian ghost [1983&#x2019;s A Pattern of Roses ] and was convinced I had something. I wasn&#x2019;t so sure. I thought I should go to university. &#x2018;Look,&#x2019; he said somewhat impatiently. &#x2018;I really am one of the top five agents in London.&#x2019; And so began one of my longest partnerships in my life. We did, I think about 20 years together. And I never did go to university. And nor did I ever train.&#x201D; Watch on Deadline if ( !window.pmc.harmony?.isEventAdScheduledTime() ) { pmcCnx.cmd.push(function() { pmcCnx({ settings: { plugins: { pmcAtlasMG: { iabPlcmt: 2, } } }, playerId: '32fe25c4-79aa-406a-af44-69b41e969e71', playlistId: '0199e506-e642-7728-8264-463efe71337b', }).render("connatix_contextual_player_div"); }); } else { // This should only be get called when page cache is not cleared and it's event time. window.pmc.harmony?.switchToHarmonyPlayer(); }

Conway wasted no time. He fired off a message to Trevor Nunn suggesting that he consider Bonham Carter for the title role in Lady Jane , Nunn&#x2019;s film about Lady Jane Grey, the 16 th -century &#x201C;Nine Days Queen&#x201D;. Next, Conway took Celestia Fox, Merchant Ivory&#x2019;s casting director for a jolly supper, where he advocated Bonham Carter for the role of Lucy Honeychurch in their upcoming production of A Room with a View . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dl-mid-article-inject2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article2","mid-articleX","mid-article","mid","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

During this period, Grant remarked, &#x201C;Jeremy represented several of each cast of the Merchant Ivory Films.&#x201D; Anthony Hopkins and Bonham Carter both starred in Howard&#x2019;s End , while Hopkins went on to make Remains of the Day . Cross-referencing the Merchant Ivory catalogue, it&#x2019;s possible to discern that, over a period of three decades, scores of CVGG artistes populated their films.

I met Conway many times over the years &#x2014; at first nights, at Oscar-night soir&#xE9;es in Hollywood &#x2014; and every now and then we&#x2019;d have lunch. He once explained that, as the son of Colonel Charles Maxwell Orr Sawers, a colonel in the 9th Royal Deccan Horse who served in India and Burma, he knew all about &#x201C;getting work done and just getting on with it.&#x201D; I found that comment from Conway in a red Silvine notebook, one of hundreds that I forgot to throw away. The army-brat background, I think, gave Conway that carpe diem attitude, but it was cloaked by his avuncular bearing.

But he was definitely getting on with it when he got his hands on Ted Tally&#x2019;s screenplay for The Silence of the Lambs . And he was getting stuff done when suggested that the film&#x2019;s director Jonathan Demme go and watch Hopkins in David Hare and Howard Brenton&#x2019;s play Pravda , which opened at London&#x2019;s National Theatre in May 1985. The part of Hannibal Lecter won Hopkins his first Academy Award.

Conway loved actors. I would often catch him at plays well into their runs, featuring thespians that he didn&#x2019;t represent. He wasn&#x2019;t out to poach them; he just wanted to watch great performances.

Born David Maxwell Sawers, Conway attended Radley College in Abingdon, in Oxford. After that, he studied drama at the Guildhall School of Music & Drama., which is where he met his life-long partner Neville Phillips, with whom he entered into a civil partnership in 2005. Parts in Z Cars , early episodes of Doctor Who and stage roles followed, but Conway enjoyed watching the likes of Judi Dench, Maggie Smith and Hopkins at the Old Vic rather more than treading the boards himself.

Deciding to become an agent, he joined forces with former Royal Academy of Dramatic Arts-trained actor-turned-agent Norman Boyack. Together they formed Boyack and Conway, where their roster included John Thaw, Sheila Hancock and Edward Hardwicke. When Boyack decided to leave the business, Conway set up on his own, representing Hopkins, Susan Penhaligon and Trudie Styler, then an actress, early on in her career.

Once Van Gelder joined, the business grew. Grant observed that Conway was &#x201C;definitely one of the first agents in London to represent European and world film actors from various countries. As wide a range as Romania, Scandinavia, Germany, France and India. Notably Jesper Christensen, Lars Mikkelsen &#x2014; who&#x2019;s still with us &#x2014; and Om Puri.&#x201D;

Aside from his film, theatre and television passions, Conway loved to cook and entertain, and he would regularly host dinner parties at the weekend, inviting the good and the great of the entertainment world. Grant added that he was a keen gardener and collector of art and artefacts. &#x201C;He was also an avid reader,&#x201D; Grant marveled, &#x201C;and somehow found time to read many books alongside a large volume of scripts. He had an encyclopedic knowledge of plays and could frequently be heard discussing why someone was specifically right for a role.&#x201D;

For over a decade Conway was a board director of the London Academy of Music and Dramatic Art, where he was first in line to scoop up tomorrow&#x2019;s stars. He was also long associated with Bafta, having been a member for 60 years. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-articleX","mid-article","btf","300x251"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .exemptFromSleep() ; });

A better-than-thriving CVGG is Conway&#x2019;s legacy; he always had one eye on the future by partnering with Van Gelder and Grant. How he went to bat for all his actors mattered most. I remember being on the set of Guy Ritchie and Matthew Vaughn&#x2019;s Lock, Stock and Two Smoking Barrels when Jason Flemyng inched his way over to me for a chat and he was almost in tears as he told how Conway had saved his life by &#x201C;giving me a career&#x201D;.

That&#x2019;s precisely the side of Conway&#x2019;s character that Bonham Carter reflected on in her tribute to her beloved agent, which I&#x2019;m posting in full below&#x2026;

&#x201C;I think for Jeremy&#x2019;s retirement party I wrote a note saying, &#x2018;Thank you for my career.&#x2019; I meant it. I don&#x2019;t think any of it would have happened if it weren&#x2019;t for him. He started it all; 42 years ago, I was 17 and sitting in Jeremy&#x2019;s office on a rather low futon or sofa watching him pace up and down in front of me in mild frustration. He had seen me in a Channel 4 drama playing an Edwardian ghost and was convinced I had something. I wasn&#x2019;t so sure. I thought I should go to university. &#x2018;Look,&#x2019; he said somewhat impatiently. &#x2018;I really am one of the top five agents in London.&#x2019; And so began one of my longest partnerships in my life. We did, I think about 20 years together. And I never did go to university. And nor did I ever train.

&#x201C;Jeremy was my industry parent. He was my champion. And patron. My enthusiast. He was bossy, impatient, and had formidable energy and appetite for all things life had to offer. He had great taste. His house, when I last saw him, was brimful of paintings and objects of beauty. He loved his job and he loved it for the culture of it &#x2014; the plays, the acting, the life, art, the people. His interest and curiosity was acute.

&#x201C;Of course, most of our relationship was conducted on the phone. He had a great, handsome, fully resonant telephone voice. He had trained as an actor and would always intone, &#x2018;CON-sonants, Helly!&#x2019;

&#x201C;One of my favorite poets, Mary Oliver, ends one of her poems, by saying, &#x2018;I don&#x2019;t want to end up having simply visited this world.&#x2019; Jeremy didn&#x2019;t just visit it, he ate it, and he tasted it. He explored, and he made people&#x2019;s careers and opened doors, and he grew an agency from seed that lives and thrives.

&#x201C;His legacy and his children are the agency and all those he impacted, people whose lives would be utterly different without him. His family of connections and tentacles of influence over decades in the industry is like a tree with many roots, an old oak that will far outlive us all.

&#x201C;I think of him with huge love and gratitude. I was all his idea. All his fault.&#x201D;

The fourth edition of Ivory Coast&#x2019;s International Salon for Audiovisual Content of Abidjan ( SICA ), running Nov. 26&#x2013;28, seeks to harness Africa&#x2019;s wealth of creative talent while addressing the structural challenges of building a sustainable audiovisual industry across the continent.

Held under the theme of content economics and cultural diplomacy, this year&#x2019;s edition comes as Ivory Coast rolls out a national strategy to improve access to financing for local producers, attract international productions through fiscal incentives and develop the infrastructure needed to support a growing industry. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘The Squirrel’ Review: An Endearing Futuristic Dramedy, Finland's Oscar Entry Makes a Case for Organic Love in the Age of Automation ‘Grand Theft Auto VI’ Review: A Bloody, Boundary-Shifting Reclamation of the American Dream

&#x201C;We have gradually moved from a simple gathering of professionals promoting their content to a real platform for reflection, cooperation and the creation of economic opportunities,&#x201D; Ivorian Minister of Communication Amadou Coulibaly, the driving force behind the annual event, tells Variety . &#x201C;We have managed to give our creations, which were previously viewed solely from a cultural perspective, real economic value.&#x201D;

A memorandum of understanding set to be signed between the public Media Support and Development Agency and Ivorian commercial bank NSIA Banque during SICA , aims to address access to financing, one of the sector&#x2019;s biggest obstacles. &#x201C;Our young people are talented, they have a lot of ideas, but there are no resources to finance those ideas,&#x201D;Coulibaly notes.

The initiative will give producers access to grants or bank loans backed by state guarantees. To finance it, the ministries of communication and culture are pooling around two billion CFA francs ($3.34 million), with a further 500 million to one billion CFA francs ($830,000&#x2013;$1.67 million) anticipated from the country&#x2019;s youth employment agency. Coulibaly estimates that financial leverage could generate between five billion and six billion CFA francs ($8.3 million&#x2013;$10 million) in guarantees. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We don&#x2019;t want it to stop at the national level,&#x201D; says Coulibaly, whose team has initiated discussions with the African Export-Import Bank (Afreximbank). &#x201C;We want this mechanism, which we are going to test in Ivory Coast, to be extended across the continent if it works.&#x201D; The pilot phase is set to begin in 2027.

Ivory Coast&#x2019;s 2027 finance bill, adopted by the National Assembly and awaiting Senate approval, includes tax and customs incentives for equipment for film production and for the construction of new cinemas. A tax credit to encourage filming in the country is also in development.

Coulibaly draws a parallel with Ivory Coast&#x2019;s position as a hub for Francophone African music in the 1980s and &#x2019;90s, attracting artists such as Salif Ke&#xEF;ta and Manu Dibango. &#x201C;We want Ivory Coast to regain, in cinema and audiovisual, the position it held in the &#x2019;80s and &#x2019;90s with music,&#x201D; he says.

Previous editions of SICA have already yielded tangible results. Franco-American producer Alex Berger brought his Arte series &#x201C;Eldorado&#x201D; to Ivory Coast after attending SICA for the first time, employing a crew that was nearly 75% Ivorian, according to Coulibaly.

The minister also reveals that American producer Larry Kasanoff , a keynote speaker last year, is developing a production with an estimated budget of $30 million&#x2013;$35 million, with the bulk of filming expected to take place in Ivory Coast.

Luc Gn&#xE9;pa&#x2019;s &#x201C;Ebinto,&#x201D; an adaptation of Amadou Kon&#xE9;&#x2019;s classic Ivorian novel, has recorded more than 50,000 admissions across Ivory Coast, Senegal and France, including a sold-out premiere at Paris&#x2019; Grand Rex. It marks the first feature film co-production for Ivorian broadcaster NCI&#x2019;s production arm, NCI Cr&#xE9;ation, the fruit of a meeting between the broadcaster and the film&#x2019;s producer, Charly Kodjo, at SICA.

&#x201C;SICA is the framework that has allowed all these projects to be born and to develop,&#x201D; he explains.

Launched last year, the SICA Business Hub connects audiovisual creators with potential investors, co-producers, broadcasters and distributors. One of its first beneficiaries, &#x201C;Na&#xEF;k&#xE9;,&#x201D; an Ivorian-Congolese co-production directed and produced by Viateur Yapo and Amida Balega, secured financing after winning SICA&#x2019;s pitching competition. Shot in both countries with an Ivorian and Congolese cast and an original score by Congolese musician Lokwa Kanza, the film has an estimated budget of 350 million CFA francs ($580,000) and will receive a private screening during this year&#x2019;s salon. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Infrastructure and training are also priorities. According to the European Audiovisual Observatory&#x2019;s FOCUS 2026 report, Ivory Coast, a country of 32 million people, had just 15 cinema screens in 2024.

Alongside the recently opened studio by Canal+, Mauritanian filmmaker Abderrahmane Sissako (&#x201C; Timbuktu &#x201D;), a SICA mainstay, is developing Treich Studio Academy, a complex housing studios, incubators, screening rooms and technical training facilities.

Ivorian actor Isaach de Bankol&#xE9; (&#x201C; The Limits of Control &#x201D;) launched his acting school initiative, Premier Continent, this October, with Cannes Film Festival head Thierry Fr&#xE9;maux attending the inauguration and pledging the festival&#x2019;s support.

&#x201C;These are training centers with a pan-African vocation,&#x201D; Coulibaly stresses. &#x201C;They are not just for Ivory Coast, they are open to the world.&#x201D;

The Ivorian government is also working with local free-to-air television channels to support domestic productions, guaranteeing an initial broadcast for projects backed by these channels. An initial round of negotiations has brought broadcasters&#x2019; exclusivity periods down from at least five years to three, with discussions underway to reduce them further, allowing producers to sell their work to other broadcasters sooner.

Content monetization on digital platforms remains another challenge, with limited opportunities for creators to earn revenue in many African countries. According to Coulibaly, discussions with Meta to address the issue are at an advanced stage, with plans to open similar negotiations with YouTube. &#x201C;Our producers must be able to benefit from the revenue generated when their works are broadcast on these platforms,&#x201D; he insists.

International cooperation remains central to SICA&#x2019;s ambitions. Alongside screenings and masterclasses from Japan, this year&#x2019;s country of honor, the salon is preparing cooperation agreements with Cameroon&#x2019;s International Audiovisual Salon (SINAC) and Senegal&#x2019;s International African Media Salon (SIMA), with further discussions involving Cairo and Red Sea film festivals underway.

Coulibaly also wants to transform SICA into a year-round platform, with sessions dedicated to financing, co-production, intellectual property rights and contract negotiations, while developing the Business Hub into a fully fledged audiovisual market over the next five years. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;We can&#x2019;t do all of this in three days,&#x201D; he says. &#x201C;There will be different sessions throughout the year, but always under the umbrella of SICA.&#x201D;

&#x201C;We have stories to tell the world,&#x201D; Coulibaly adds. &#x201C;It is important that we take ownership of our own stories, that we manage to build our own narrative, translate it into films and share it with the world.&#x201D;

Candace Cameron Bure appeared on the &#x201C; McBride Rewind &#x201D; podcast on Tuesday and discussed the &#x201C;substantial&#x201D; residuals she still gets from &#x201C; Full House ,&#x201D; as well as why she wasn&#x2019;t surprised that Mary-Kate and Ashley Olsen didn&#x2019;t return for the hit sitcom&#x2019;s spin-off, &#x201C;Fuller House.&#x201D;

&#x201C;They&#x2019;re substantial&#x2026; I think it&#x2019;s like quarterly,&#x201D; Bure told host Josh McBride of the consistency of her &#x201C;Full House&#x201D; residuals, adding that every check is different, but &#x201C;still substantial.&#x201D; &#x201C;I&#x2019;m always happy when I open that check and deposit it,&#x201D; she added. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories ‘Best Pancakes in the County’ Review: Nicolas Cage Stars in a Thriller You Could Fairly Describe as Tarantino Lite 'The Gospel of Christmas' Review: Tyler Perry's Churchy Musical Drama Does a Threadbare Job of Getting Into the Spirit

McBride then brought up Bure's &#x201C;Full House&#x201D; co-star Jodie Sweetin , who made in April when the actress revealed she&#x2019;d received a &#x201C;one-cent check&#x201D; from the show on the podcast. &#x201C;She said she doesn&#x2019;t get much now,&#x201D; Bure said. &#x201C;And I was like, &#x2018;Jodie, you gotta check with your agent or you gotta call your bank.&#x2019; &#x2019;Cause I still get residuals.&#x201D;

Speaking of the Olsen twins, Bure said that their decision not to appear on &#x201C;Fuller House&#x201D; was &#x201C;a bummer&#x201D; because &#x201C;it would have been fun to have everybody back.&#x201D; &#x201C;But at the same time, it wasn&#x2019;t surprising just because none of us really have stayed close with the girls,&#x201D; Bure noted.

She continued: &#x201C;Not because anything went wrong or there was any bad blood. I just think they were kids. They were [filming from] 9 months old until they were 8 years old. They have very different memories than we do. Even me being 10 years older than them, I have significant, great, wonderful memories.&#x201D;

&#x201C;They were babies. They probably don&#x2019;t even remember half the stuff [we do],&#x201D; she added. &#x201C;They didn&#x2019;t have the attachment to the crew and the people like we did being older. And they had such a successful fashion business. They haven&#x2019;t been actors for a long time. They just haven&#x2019;t been in that part of entertainment.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Sweetin played Stephanie Tanner and Bure played D.J. Tanner on &#x201C;Full House,&#x201D; which ran for eight seasons from 1987 to 1995. &#x201C;Fuller House&#x201D; ran for five seasons on Netflix, totaling nearly 80 episodes. Original cast members, including Bure, Sweetin, Andrea Barber, Scott Weinger, Bob Saget, Lori Loughlin, Dave Coulier and John Stamos, all returned for the series. Juan Pablo Di Pace, Adam Hagenbuch, John Brotherton, Michael Campion, Elias Harger and Soni Bringas also starred in the reboot.

In the sixth and final episode of &#x201C; South Park &#x201D; Season 29, South America has once again been hit with major power outages &#x2014; but this time it&#x2019;s serious, considering &#x201C;Grand Theft Auto VI&#x201D; has finally been released, which means the residents of the mountain town will stop at nothing to restore their Xboxes and PlayStations and continue playing the long-awaited video game.

&#x201C;Damn it, Mayor! We have waited over a decade for this game to come out,&#x201D; proclaims one angry South American resident at the top of the episode. &#x201C;Do you have any idea how &#x2018;Grand Theft Auto VI&#x2019; works? If it shuts up while it's saving or during a mission, you lose everything.&#x201D; The issue, though, is that the South American government has made a deal with a group of billionaire weenies, as was introduced in the season&#x2019;s second episode, who are using the town&#x2019;s energy to power their data centers. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Ceremony Gets Fired Up With Live-Wire Numbers From U2, the Chili Peppers, Usher, Cynthia Erivo, Sienna Spiro, Aerosmith and More Rock & Roll Hall of Fame Designates the Troubadour as a Landmark Venue; Going Forward, L.A. Will Host Hall's Induction Ceremony 'At Least Every Other Year' (EXCLUSIVE)

The town's politicians have no idea what to do about the issue, but luckily for them, a group of angry townspeople barge into South American City Hall and proclaim they know who's behind the outages: the Chinese. More specifically, the outages are the result of Chinese cyberattacks. Relieved, the town&#x2019;s politicians let them believe this is the case &#x2014; &#x201C;Yes, you figured it out. It's definitely cyber attacks by the Chinese&#x201D; &#x2014; as they begin to search for a Chinese spy who must be living in South America.

But Butters has known the billionaires were to blame since the beginning, and confides in Stan, Kyle and Cartman. Oh, and a zombified Kenny (who got blown up by an e-bike during the season&#x2019;s premiere) also makes a few appearances. Turns out, Kenny&#x2019;s spirit can&#x2019;t move on until the group figures out what's going on and exposes all the corruption in South America &#x2014; great timing for them, as they&#x2019;ve all learned about the data centers and are ready to make a change. The gang takes this revelation to City Hall, where the politicians explain how it all began &#x201C;with those damn e-bikes&#x201D; and fear that the group of kids is going to blow their secret deal with the billionaires. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

But it wasn&#x2019;t an e-bike that killed Kenny, says a still shrunken Randy who barges into City Hall. &#x201C;We all did. We all share in the blame equally&#x2026; When they changed the name of our town, we let it change us. We used force, took bribes, looked the other way, because we let them change South Park.&#x201D;

In the end, the mayor of South American addresses the town and owns up to her mistakes &#x2014; kind of.

&#x201C;I owe you all an apology. Since the town changed its name, I've taken bribes. I've looked the other way, and I did make a deal with billionaires,&#x201D; she says. &#x201C;But I've learned that even though we must build data centers because there is a very real threat from the Chinese in the AI arms race, we can't let that change who we are.&#x201D;

And so, the billionaire weenies help the town &#x201C;do something we should have done a long time ago&#x201D;: shoot Mr. Kim into space and out of South America. And with that, another season of "South Park" (and the first season with the new name of "South America") comes to a close.

